### Global Variables and Standalone Functions

#### Global Variables

- **`n`**: An integer representing the number of elements in the input array.
- **`log2n`**: An integer representing the logarithm base 2 of `n`.
- **`i`**: A loop counter variable.
- **`count`**: A long long integer representing the cumulative sum of the array elements.

#### Standalone Functions

- **`std::cin >> n`**: Reads the number of elements `n` from the standard input.
